# pagesflow documentation sync

When you modify a routed page or its direct child components, update the matching `pagesflow/<folder>/PAGE.md` in the same change.

## Route → folder mapping

Use the index in `pagesflow/README.md`. Common mappings:

| Source | Docs |
|--------|------|
| `pages/Login.tsx` | `pagesflow/login/PAGE.md` |
| `pages/Signup.tsx` | `pagesflow/signup/PAGE.md` |
| `pages/Onboarding.tsx` + `components/onboarding/*` | `pagesflow/onboarding/PAGE.md` |
| `pages/ForgotPasswordPage.tsx` | `pagesflow/forgot-password/PAGE.md` |
| `pages/AccountSettings.tsx` | `pagesflow/account-settings/PAGE.md` |
| `pages/Dashboard.tsx` | `pagesflow/dashboard/PAGE.md` |
| `components/notifications/*` | `pagesflow/notifications/PAGE.md` |

## What to update in PAGE.md

- Fields table (required vs optional, validation, position)
- Actions and redirects
- API endpoints (frontend → middleware → Java)
- File map if paths changed
- Mermaid sequence diagram if flow changed
- Edge cases

## Env changes

If the page depends on new or changed env vars, also update `pagesflow/mandatory-fields.md`.

## Template

New pages: copy `pagesflow/_TEMPLATE.md` and add a row to `pagesflow/README.md`.
